Imports:
  - Types:
      - LazyLoader
    From: salt/loader

Annotations: |
  This cell is salt/cache — a small, cleanly-layered plugin category: a single `Cache` facade
  class (with an in-process-memory specialization, `MemCache`) whose actual storage operations
  are delegated to a dynamically-dispatched backend driver module, selected by the cache
  config option (default localfs) and loaded on demand via salt.loader.cache (tag
  "cache"). The driver-module relationship is modeled here with the DSL's mutation notation
  (Cache::LocalFSBackend) because it is a real concretization-without-inheritance pattern: the
  driver is a plain module of same-named functions dynamically dispatched through a `LazyLoader`,
  not a Python subclass of `Cache`.

---

"Cache(opts: dict[str, object], cachedir: str | None)":
  location: __init__.py
  annotations: |
    Salt's general-purpose key/value cache facade, organized as banks (like directories) each
    holding keys (like files). Used for the minion data cache, the master's job cache, and ad hoc
    caching needs across the codebase.

    `opts`: the Salt options dictionary; opts["cache"] selects the backend driver (default
    localfs)
    cachedir: root directory for the default on-disk backend; defaults from opts["cachedir"]
  properties:
    "modules -> LazyLoader": |
      The backend-driver `LazyLoader` (tag "cache", from salt.loader.cache), computed once and
      cached; store/fetch/flush/list/contains all dispatch through this.
  methods:
    "store(bank: str, key: str, data: object, expires: int | None)": |
      Write `data` under `key` in `bank` via the configured backend driver.

      `bank`: cache namespace, e.g. minions/<id>/data
      `key`: entry name within `bank`
      `expires`: if the backend driver doesn't natively support expiry, wrap `data` with an
      _expires timestamp for manual expiry checking on read
    "fetch(bank: str, key: str) -> data:object": |
      Read back the value previously stored under `key` in `bank`, or a falsy/empty value if
      absent.
    "flush(bank: str, key: str | None)": |
      Remove `key` from `bank`, or the entire `bank` if `key` is omitted.
    "list(bank: str) -> keys:list[str]": |
      List the keys currently present in `bank`.
    "contains(bank: str, key: str | None) -> present:bool": |
      Report whether `key` exists in `bank` (or whether `bank` itself exists, if `key` is
      omitted).

"Cache::MemCache()":
  location: __init__.py
  annotations: |
    An in-process memory layer in front of the same backend driver, active when
    memcache_expire_seconds is configured (selected by salt.cache.factory). Overrides
    fetch/store/flush to check/populate a per-process memory store before/after delegating
    to the underlying driver, with its own independent expiry.

"Cache::LocalFSBackend()":
  location: localfs.py
  annotations: |
    The default cache backend driver: implements the same store/fetch/flush operations as
    plain on-disk file operations under a per-cachedir directory tree, dispatched dynamically
    through Cache.modules rather than through inheritance.
  methods:
    "store(bank: str, key: str, data: object, cachedir: str)": |
      Serialize `data` and write it to the on-disk path derived from `bank`/`key` under
      cachedir.
    "fetch(bank: str, key: str, cachedir: str) -> data:object": |
      Read and deserialize the on-disk entry for `bank`/`key`, or an empty value if it doesn't
      exist.
    "flush(bank: str, key: str | None, cachedir: str | None)": |
      Delete the on-disk entry for `key` in `bank` (or the whole `bank` directory if `key` is
      omitted).

